#: ../../whatsnew/3.8.rst:535
msgid ""
"The :meth:`object.__reduce__` method can now return a tuple from two to six "
"elements long. Formerly, five was the limit.  The new, optional sixth "
"element is a callable with a ``(obj, state)`` signature.  This allows the "
"direct control over the state-updating behavior of a specific object.  If "
"not *None*, this callable will have priority over the "
"object's :meth:`~object.__setstate__` method. (Contributed by Pierre Glaser "
"and Olivier Grisel in :issue:`35900`.)"
msgstr ""
"Die Methode :meth:`object.__reduce__` kann nun ein Tupel mit zwei bis sechs "
"Elementen zurückgeben. Bisher lag die Grenze bei fünf. Das neue, optionale "
